            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Someone needs to look at this with a better understanding of boost yield_context coroutines.  I can't get this to pass on both 1.87 and 1.86 with the same code, nor do I understand it enough to figure out if this is a boost bug we need to file.\n\nSo far as I can tell, to support c++20 coroutines boost::asio::spawn added the ability to potentially return a co_return object.  Because of this, the prototype of spawn became no_discard.  When used with yield_context coroutines, the return type of boost::asio::spawn is void (80% sure of this), but with no_discard, we need to explicitly [[maybe_unused]] the \"returned\" void value.\n\nIf we capture that to a variable, boost 1.86 fails to build (because it actually returns void).  If we don't capture, we fail the nodiscard check on 1.87."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Jasons Idea was better than mine.  I tried to get too modern"
                }
            ],
